  "case_order_and_prerequisite": "Run the excluded calibration first; require actual normalized PCM identity, one CPU pass, exact9/4/0/264/264/222 config, finite0..1eight-channel probabilities, floor(N/160)+1native frames and matching saved HF/Q8 geometry before either unchanged target. Preserve any failure logs/partial outputs. Calibration is not a claimed numerical-equality acceptance test.",
  "comparison_rules": [
    "One fresh native process/session per case, repetitions1 and requestedGPU=-1, exact recorded qualified CPU package. No graph/cache/input/segmentation override besides the already-frozen geometry.",
    "Native output has floor(N/160)+1rows; saved HF has floor(N/160). Compare native F32/HF and saved native Q8/HF only on the common valid prefix; preserve the native terminal row separately and compare F32/Q8 over every raw row.",
    "No speaker relabeling or per-chunk frame matching. Compare corresponding eight learned output channels. Report maximum/mean/RMS/p95/p99 probability differences, first unequal/worst frame and speaker channel, bitwise identity and both terminal vectors.",
    "Zero comparison tolerance describes inequality only. There is no newly selected probability/DER quality cutoff, no scoring, tuning, pruning of hard frames or claim a descriptive small mean proves model equivalence.",
    "Require frozen helper RPATH\u2192canonical package binding and full existing CPU package verification before inference; verify all model/library/WAV/original inference bytes again after execution."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Already-seen targets; not fresh heldout validation. Original frozen DER/reference/scorer/protocol/model locks and failures remain unchanged.",
    "The original .nemo source stores363BF16tensors; the published HF safetensors header stores417F32tensors. Native control upcasts the .nemo values toF32 except one F16 convolution, and the saved HF run executes CPU FP32. No missing .nemo source precision is recovered and this is not an all-FP32 native artifact. Full HF-versus-.nemo source-weight mapping remains a distinct verification boundary.",
    "Native and HF use different filterbank values as measured separately; this free-running comparison includes frontend arithmetic/bank, graph and cache effects. Does not isolate each contribution or establish original-NeMo equivalence.",
    "No production-model replacement, quantization selection, postprocessing change, CPU/Metal claim, uncontended timing claim or release qualification.",
    "No HF/original-NeMo model rerun; saved official HF CPU arrays are reused. Native NN execution is new and explicitly labeled."
  ],
